%% ============================================
%% APPENDIX F: THE TEN "DO YOU NOT KNOW" QUESTIONS
%% ============================================
\chapter*{Appendix F: ``Do You Not Know?'' --- 1 Corinthians' Signature Rhetorical Question 「你們豈不知道」——哥林多前書的詰問風格}
\addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{Appendix F: ``Do You Not Know?'' --- 1 Corinthians' Signature Rhetorical Question 「你們豈不知道」——哥林多前書的詰問風格}

\begin{small}
哥林多前書在保羅書信中，以反覆使用「你們豈不知道」（οὐκ οἴδατε, ouk oidate）這句詰問著稱——全卷共出現十次，比新約任何一卷書都多。這不是修辭上的巧合，而是一種一貫的教導策略：保羅不是在傳遞哥林多人所不知道的新知識，而是提醒他們早已領受、卻在生活中忘記了的身分與事實。
\textit{First Corinthians is distinctive among Paul's letters for its repeated use of the rhetorical question ``Do you not know'' (οὐκ οἴδατε, ouk oidate) --- occurring ten times, more than any other New Testament book. This is not rhetorical coincidence but a consistent teaching strategy: Paul is not delivering new information the Corinthians lack, but reminding them of an identity and a set of facts they had already received, yet had forgotten to live out of.}
\end{small}

\vspace{0.3cm}

\begin{small}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.4}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{1.4cm}p{2.7in}p{2.4in}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{經文} & \textbf{中文} & \textbf{English} \\
\midrule
3:16 & 豈不知你們是神的殿，神的靈住在你們裏頭嗎？ & Do you not know that you are God's temple and that God's Spirit dwells in you? \\
5:6 & 豈不知一點麵酵能使全團發起來嗎？ & Do you not know that a little leaven leavens the whole lump? \\
6:2 & 豈不知聖徒要審判世界嗎？ & Do you not know that the saints will judge the world? \\
6:3 & 豈不知我們要審判天使嗎？ & Do you not know that we are to judge angels? \\
6:9 & 你們豈不知不義的人不能承受神的國嗎？ & Do you not know that the unrighteous will not inherit the kingdom of God? \\
6:15 & 豈不知你們的身體是基督的肢體嗎？ & Do you not know that your bodies are members of Christ? \\
6:16 & 豈不知與娼妓聯合的，就是與她成為一體嗎？ & Do you not know that he who is joined to a prostitute becomes one body with her? \\
6:19 & 豈不知你們的身體就是聖靈的殿嗎？ & Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit within you? \\
9:13 & 你們豈不知在殿裏事奉的吃殿裏的食物嗎？ & Do you not know that those who are employed in the temple service get their food from the temple? \\
9:24 & 你們不知道在運動場上賽跑的都跑，但得獎的只有一人嗎？ & Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize? \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{small}

\vspace{0.4cm}

\begin{small}
這十次詰問，沒有一次是要告訴哥林多人一件全新的事；每一次，保羅都只是把他們已經領受、卻已經忘記活出來的身分重新喚回——你們是神的殿、你們的身體是基督的肢體、你們將來要審判世界。問題從來不是「不知道」，而是「忘記了」；這正呼應全書「領受」的主軸：不是缺乏資訊，而是被遺忘的、卻早已屬乎自己的身分，需要被重新喚醒。\\
\textit{Not one of these ten questions tells the Corinthians something new; each time, Paul simply calls back to mind an identity they had already received but had stopped living out of --- that they are God's temple, that their bodies are members of Christ, that they will one day judge the world. The problem was never ignorance, but forgetfulness --- which matches the letter's larger emphasis on reception: not new information, but a forgotten identity being called back to mind.}
\end{small}

